Package: panelart
Type: Package
Title: Atheoretical Regression Trees for Common Breaks in Panels of Time Series
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Marco", "Reale", email = "marco.reale@canterbury.ac.nz", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Detects common structural breaks in a panel of time series by
    pooled least squares. For breaks in the mean it implements classic greedy
    binary regression trees with BIC or cost-complexity pruning (atheoretical
    regression trees, Rea, Reale, Cappelli and Brown (2010)
    <doi:10.1080/07474938.2010.482001>) and an extended estimator with a
    forward-repartition-eliminate cycle, hull-merge thinning, penalties
    calibrated by Monte Carlo or from long-run covariance estimates, whitening
    and factor projection. For continuous piecewise-linear trends it provides
    a join-point estimator with options for serially and cross-sectionally
    dependent errors. Limit-law confidence intervals and simulation utilities
    for Monte Carlo studies are included.
License: GPL (>= 2)
URL: https://github.com/MarcoNZreal/panelart
